## 4. Router Configuration

The following commands configure the interfaces and OSPF routing on each router.

The FastEthernet modules used in this topology operate as Layer 2 switchports. Therefore, IP addresses are assigned to VLAN interfaces instead of directly to the physical FastEthernet ports.

### 4.1 Router R1 Configuration

```cisco
enable
configure terminal

hostname R1

! VLAN 12
interface vlan 12
 ip address 10.10.12.1 255.255.255.0
 no shutdown
exit

! FastEthernet connection to R2
interface fastEthernet 0/3/0
 switchport mode access
 switchport access vlan 12
 no shutdown
exit

! GigabitEthernet connection to R3
interface gigabitEthernet 0/0
 ip address 10.10.13.1 255.255.255.0
 no shutdown
exit

! Serial connection to R4
interface serial 0/2/0
 ip address 10.10.14.1 255.255.255.0
 no shutdown
exit

! OSPF Configuration
router ospf 1
 router-id 1.1.1.1
 network 10.10.12.0 0.0.0.255 area 0
 network 10.10.13.0 0.0.0.255 area 0
 network 10.10.14.0 0.0.0.255 area 0
exit

end
copy running-config startup-config
```

