## 18. Conclusion

This project demonstrates the implementation of a single-area OSPF network using four Cisco routers interconnected through GigabitEthernet, FastEthernet, and Serial interfaces.

The lab combines Layer 2 VLAN configuration with Layer 3 routing and demonstrates how OSPF discovers neighbors, learns remote networks, and selects paths based on routing cost.

One of the key technical challenges was the advertisement of a Loopback interface as a `/24` network instead of the default `/32` host route. This was resolved using the OSPF point-to-point network type on the Loopback interface.

The lab also illustrates the importance of correct IP addressing, unique OSPF Router IDs, VLAN-to-interface mapping, and systematic troubleshooting.

Overall, the project provides hands-on experience with fundamental routing and switching concepts used in enterprise IP networks.


